# Database models and migrations

Paths are under `src/` unless noted.

## SQLAlchemy / ORM

- Define tables and mapped classes **only** in `models/` (e.g. `models/user/`, `models/content/`).
- Do **not** define ORM mapped classes in `lib/`, HTTP route modules, or Alembic revision files.

## SQLModel class set per entity (SQLModel in `models/`)

For each persisted entity, use this naming and split (same module file is fine):

| Class | Role |
|-------|------|
| `{Entity}Base` | Shared non-table fields (payload shape). No `table=True`. |
| `{Entity}Create` | Insert payload; extends `Base` where useful. No `table=True`. |
| `{Entity}Update` | PATCH-style optional fields. No `table=True`. |
| `{Entity}Delete` | Delete result / confirmation shape if you use one. No `table=True`. |
| `{Entity}Read` | Outbound API row shape (may include `id` / FK values as **plain types**). No `table=True`. |
| `{Entity}` | **The only mapped table class** — `..., table=True`, `__tablename__`, mixins as needed. |

**Keys and persistence-only `Field(...)` options** — `primary_key`, `foreign_key`, relationships, and DB-oriented `unique` / `index` (anything that exists for the physical table) — **only** on `{Entity}` (`table=True`). Non-table classes may use validation-oriented options (e.g. `max_length`); they must not declare PKs, FKs, or table-level uniqueness/indexes that belong on the ORM row.

## Alembic

- **Do not** manually edit, rewrite, or hand-author revision files under `alembic/versions/` (e.g. `src/alembic/versions/*.py`). New revisions are produced only by Alembic **autogenerate** from ORM metadata.
- To change the database, update **`models/`** and **enums** that affect the schema (`lib/enums/` or legacy `src/enums/` until migrated), then run the project’s autogenerate command—**never** patch migration files by hand in the editor.

## Quick reference

| Topic | Rule |
|-------|------|
| ORM definitions | `models/` only |
| Migration files | Autogenerated only; do not hand-edit `alembic/versions/` |
| Schema changes | `models/` + DB-affecting enums, then autogenerate |
| Entity class set | `Base`, `Create`, `Update`, `Delete`, `Read`, then `{Entity}` table |
| PK / FK / DB indexes | Only on `{Entity}` (`table=True`), not on other five |
